cff-version: 1.2.0
title: RecoilLab
message: >
  If you use this software in research, teaching material,
  presentations, or publications, please cite the repository.

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Davini
    given-names: Stefano
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3269-1718

repository-code: https://github.com/<github-user>/DMRecoilLab

license: BSD-3-Clause

keywords:
  - dark matter
  - direct detection
  - WIMP
  - nuclear recoils
  - particle physics
  - astroparticle physics
  - phenomenology

abstract: >
  RecoilLab is a modular Python framework for dark matter
  direct-detection calculations. The package provides tools
  for halo modelling, scattering kinematics, nuclear response
  functions, interaction models, detector modelling,
  recoil-spectrum calculations, and sensitivity studies
  with a focus on physical transparency, reproducibility, and education.

version: 0.1.0

date-released: 2026-10-06